invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">PRODUIT MIXTE TEINT CONSTITUE D'UNE FIBRE APTE A LA TEINTURE AVEC UN COLORANT DISPERSE ET D'UNE FIBRE DE POLYURETHANNE, ET PROCEDE DE TEINTURE APPROPRIE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-11172584-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11172584</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="AP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-4041754-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>4041754</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-4185713-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>4185713</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5279971-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5279971</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5295673-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5295673</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6294078-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6294078</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8209554-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8209554</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9324346-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9324346</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1152083A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA KIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI KASEI KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA KIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A blended product of a fiber dyeable with a disperse dye and a polyurethane fiber having been dyed with a disperse dye which exhibits a fastness to sweat and alkali of 3 degree according to JIS L-0848-A, has high color fastness and has a surface dyeing depth of 20 or less in terms of L value in spectrocalorimetry. The dyed blended product with a polyurethane fiber can be prepared by pretreating a mixed fabric, such as knitted fabric, of a fiber dyeable with a disperse dye and a polyurethane fiber with a dye bath solution containing a poly-valent metal compound and tannic acid prior to dyeing with a disperse dye or by dyeing it using a dye bath containing a poly-valent metal compound and tannic acid together with a disperse dye.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un produit mixte constitué d'une fibre apte à la teinture avec un colorant dispersé et d'une fibre de polyuréthanne teinte avec un colorant dispersé. Ce produit présente une résistance à la sueur et aux alcalis de 3 degrés selon JIS L-0848-A, une grande solidité des couleurs et une profondeur de teinture à la pointe inférieure ou égale à 20 en termes de valeur L en spectrocalorimétrie. Ce produit mixte teinté contenant une fibre de polyuréthanne peut être préparé par prétraitement d'un tissu mixte, par exemple un tissu tricoté, contenant une fibre apte à la teinture avec un colorant dispersé et une fibre de polyuréthanne, avec une solution de bain de teinture contenant un composé métallique polyvalent et de l'acide tannique, avant la teinture avec un colorant dispersé ou par teinture avec un bain de teinture contenant un composé métallique polyvalent et de l'acide tannique avec un colorant dispersé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>